  "salt": "MvAUiQpvMqr7A-sgZoGweA==",
  "text": "Ceridwen is a Welsh goddess who lived on an island in Lake Bala, in north Wales. Her name also appears as Caridwen, Cerridwen, Cariadwen, and Keridwen. People sometimes called her a witch or sorceress. She shared the island with her partner Tegid Voel. Their two children were Creirwy and Afagddu. Creirwy was beautiful, which her name means. Afagddu was called the ugliest little boy in the world. Ceridwen planned to make her son a seer. She brewed a secret mixture of herbs to grant him wisdom. The brew had to simmer in her cauldron for a year and a day. A boy named Gwion stirred the cauldron. Three drops of the brew spilled onto his thumb, and he licked them off. He gained all the wisdom meant for Afagddu. Ceridwen chased him in anger. Gwion turned into a hare, a fish, a bird, and then a grain of wheat. She turned into a greyhound, an otter, a hawk, and then a hen. The hen swallowed the grain of wheat. Ceridwen later gave birth to a child she first set adrift on the sea. That child grew to become the bard Taliesin.",
